# Cursor Rules for Euthopiar

# CRITICAL SECURITY & KEY INTEGRITY (DO NOT TOUCH)
- NEVER touch, modify, mock, or sanitize API keys in any of these files under ANY circumstance unless explicitly ordered by user:
  - core/src/main/java/com/euthopiar/core/util/TmdbBridge.kt
  - core/src/main/java/com/euthopiar/core/js/host/HostFunctions.kt
  - core/src/main/java/com/euthopiar/core/subtitle/external/SubDlClient.kt
  - core/src/main/java/com/euthopiar/core/sync/simkl/SimklClient.kt
  - core/src/main/java/com/euthopiar/core/sync/trakt/TraktClient.kt
- API keys will be moved to Cloudflare Workers in an upcoming dedicated vibe-coding session. Keep them 100% intact and working.

# CODEBASE ARCHITECTURE
- Android Project with two primary modules:
  - `core/`: Kotlin JVM/Multiplatform library module (JS QuickJS runtime, OkHttp/DohDns networking, streams, subtitles, sync providers).
  - `app/`: Android application module (Jetpack Compose UI, ExoPlayer, DownloadEngine, preferences).
- DO NOT move or rename Kotlin packages, source directories, or classes. The project builds cleanly with `gradlew.bat assembleDebug`.
- Match existing Kotlin idioms and Jetpack Compose state conventions.

# ROOT HYGIENE
- NEVER create temporary scripts, test files, screenshots, or logs in the project root (`C:\Euthopiar\`).
- If you need to write temporary test scripts, place them in `scratch/` or clean them up immediately after use.

# VERIFICATION BEFORE COMPLETION
- Always verify your work by running `./gradlew.bat assembleDebug` and ensuring `BUILD SUCCESSFUL`.
- See `AI_RULES.md` for full architectural details.
